{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "arg", "ucas": "arg 1 + i", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "arg", "input": "1 + i", "result": "pi/4"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "value", "points": 1, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "arg(1 + i) = pi/4\n  the principal argument, -pi < arg <= pi\n  check: equal numerically (0.7853981634, complex arithmetic)\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "polar", "ucas": "polar x + i y", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "polar", "input": "x + i y", "exponential": "sqrt(x^2 + y^2)*e^(i*atan2(y, x))", "trigonometric": "sqrt(x^2 + y^2)*(cos(atan2(y, x)) + i*sin(atan2(y, x)))", "r": "sqrt(x^2 + y^2)", "theta": "atan2(y, x)"}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "sample_points", "points": 64, "max_diff": 4.446160667710841e-16, "passed": true}, {"kind": "sample_points", "points": 64, "max_diff": 4.446160667710841e-16, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real\nx + i y = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)*e^(i*atan2(y, x))\n  = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)*(cos(atan2(y, x)) + i*sin(atan2(y, x)))\n  r = |z| = sqrt(x^2 + y^2),  theta = arg z = atan2(y, x)\n  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi; undefined where x = y = 0\n  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 4e-16)\n  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 4e-16)\n"}
{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "trig", "ucas": "trig sin(x) cos(x)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "trig", "input": "sin(x) cos(x)", "forms": [{"label": "product to sum", "identity": "sin a cos b = (sin(a + b) + sin(a - b))/2, cos a cos b = (cos(a - b) + cos(a + b))/2, sin a sin b = (cos(a - b) - cos(a + b))/2", "result": "sin(2x)/2", "checked": true, "check_points": 64}, {"label": "exponential (Euler)", "identity": "sin u = (e^(iu) - e^(-iu))/(2i), cos u = (e^(iu) + e^(-iu))/2", "result": "(exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))*(exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))/(4*i)", "checked": true, "check_points": 64}], "simplest": "sin(2x)/2"}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "x is taken as real"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "sample_points", "points": 64, "max_diff": 5.551115123125783e-17, "passed": true}, {"kind": "sample_points", "points": 64, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  note: x is taken as real\ntrig forms of sin(x) cos(x)\n  product to sum: sin a cos b = (sin(a + b) + sin(a - b))/2, cos a cos b = (cos(a - b) + cos(a + b))/2, sin a sin b = (cos(a - b) - cos(a + b))/2\n    = sin(2x)/2\n    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 6e-17)\n  exponential (Euler): sin u = (e^(iu) - e^(-iu))/(2i), cos u = (e^(iu) + e^(-iu))/2\n    = (exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))*(exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))/(4*i)\n    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points\n  simplest: sin(2x)/2  (product to sum)\n"}
{"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "trig", "ucas": "trig 3 sin x + 4 cos x harmonic", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "trig", "input": "3 sin x + 4 cos x", "forms": [{"label": "amplitude-phase", "identity": "a sin u + b cos u = R sin(u + phi), R = sqrt(a^2 + b^2), phi = atan2(b, a)", "result": "5sin(x + atan(4/3))", "checked": true, "check_points": 64}, {"label": "amplitude-phase", "identity": "a sin u + b cos u = R cos(u - psi), psi = atan2(a, b)", "result": "5cos(x - atan(3/4))", "checked": true, "check_points": 64}], "simplest": "3 sin x + 4 cos x"}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "x is taken as real"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "sample_points", "points": 64, "max_diff": 7.771561172376096e-16, "passed": true}, {"kind": "sample_points", "points": 64, "max_diff": 1.0269562977782698e-15, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  note: x is taken as real\ntrig forms of 3 sin x + 4 cos x\n  amplitude-phase: a sin u + b cos u = R sin(u + phi), R = sqrt(a^2 + b^2), phi = atan2(b, a)\n    = 5sin(x + atan(4/3))\n    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 8e-16)\n  amplitude-phase: a sin u + b cos u = R cos(u - psi), psi = atan2(a, b)\n    = 5cos(x - atan(3/4))\n    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 1e-15)\n  simplest: 3 sin x + 4 cos x  (as given)\n"}
{"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "holomorphic", "ucas": "holomorphic z^2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "holomorphic", "var": "z", "holomorphic": true, "entire": true}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "cauchy_riemann", "points": 64, "max_diff": 5.556038400417219e-12, "passed": true, "text": "df/dx = df/(i dy) at sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2]"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\n  holomorphic: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  entire: holomorphic on the whole plane\n"}
{"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "holomorphic", "ucas": "holomorphic conj(z)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "holomorphic", "var": "z", "holomorphic": false, "counterexample": {"at": "1/2 + i/4", "df_dx": "1", "df_idy": "-1"}, "non_holomorphic_parts": "conj"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nconj(z) is not holomorphic\n  Cauchy-Riemann fails: at z = 1/2 + i/4, df/dx = 1 but df/(i dy) = -1\n  (it uses conj, which is not holomorphic)\n  Wirtinger derivatives there: df/dz = 0, df/dconj(z) = 1 (holomorphic means df/dconj(z) = 0)\n"}
{"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "zeros", "ucas": "zeros z^2 + 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zeros", "var": "z", "polynomial": true, "degree": 2, "zeros": [{"value": "-i", "re": 0, "im": -1, "multiplicity": 1}, {"value": "i", "re": 0, "im": 1, "multiplicity": 1}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "Durand-Kerner on the polynomial's coefficients (from 64 samples, checked at 8 other points); the degree counts the roots"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nzeros of z^2 + 1 (z complex):\n  2 roots (a polynomial of degree 2):\n    z = -i\n    z = i\n  check: z^2 + 1 = 0 at the roots; the polynomial's coefficients come from 64 samples and were checked at 8 other points\n  a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 complex roots counted with multiplicity (the fundamental theorem of algebra)\n"}
{"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "residue", "ucas": "residue 1/(z^2 + 1) at i", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "residue", "var": "z", "at": "i", "found": true, "residue": "-i/2", "re": 0, "im": -0.5000000000000001, "singularity": "pole", "order": 1}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "circle_integrals", "points": 1024, "passed": true, "text": "radius 0.01 and 0.005 agree"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of 1/(z^2 + 1) at z = i:\n  = -i/2\n  a pole of order 1 (|f| grows like |z - a|^-1)\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of 1/(z^2 + 1) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}
{"id": 12, "ok": true, "cmd": "poles", "ucas": "poles 1/(z^2 + 1)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "poles", "var": "z", "poles": [{"at": "-i", "order": 1, "residue": "i/2"}, {"at": "i", "order": 1, "residue": "-i/2"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "default", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/(z^2 + 1):\n    z = -i  order 1, residue i/2\n    z = i  order 1, residue -i/2\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}
{"id": 13, "ok": true, "cmd": "integrate", "ucas": "integrate 1/z around |z| = 1", "structured": false, "result": {"text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nintegral of 1/z around |z| = 1 (counterclockwise):\n  = 2pi*i\n  numerically: the trapezoid rule on the circle with 1024 and 2048 points (difference 3e-18)\n  residue theorem: 2 pi i times the sum of the residues at the 1 pole inside = 2pi*i: agrees\n"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nintegral of 1/z around |z| = 1 (counterclockwise):\n  = 2pi*i\n  numerically: the trapezoid rule on the circle with 1024 and 2048 points (difference 3e-18)\n  residue theorem: 2 pi i times the sum of the residues at the 1 pole inside = 2pi*i: agrees\n"}
{"id": 14, "ok": true, "cmd": "monotonic", "ucas": "monotonic x^3 - 3x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "monotonic", "var": "x", "verdict": "not monotonic", "on": "all real x", "intervals": [{"lo": null, "hi": -1, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": -1, "hi": 1, "direction": "decreasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": 1, "hi": null, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}], "witness_not_decreasing": [-2, -1], "witness_not_increasing": [-1, 1]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "proved symbolically: x^3 - 3x' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity"}, "files": [], "text": "monotonic x^3 - 3x:\n  not monotonic on all real x\n  maximal intervals of monotonicity:\n    x in (-inf, -1]: increasing\n    x in [-1, 1]: decreasing\n    x in [1, inf): increasing\n  witness: x = -2 < x = -1 but f(-2) = -2 < f(-1) = 2 (not decreasing)\n  witness: x = -1 < x = 1 but f(-1) = 2 > f(1) = -2 (not increasing)\n  proved symbolically: x^3 - 3x' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity\n"}
{"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "monotonic", "ucas": "monotonic (x: u8) * 3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "monotonic", "var": "x", "verdict": "not monotonic", "on": "0..255", "intervals": [{"lo": 0, "hi": 85, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": 85, "hi": 86, "direction": "decreasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": 86, "hi": 170, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": 170, "hi": 171, "direction": "decreasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": 171, "hi": 255, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}], "witness_not_decreasing": [0, 1], "witness_not_increasing": [85, 86]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "without wrapping (as int) it is strictly increasing; the machine type wraps: f(85) = 255, f(86) = 2"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "proved, exhaustive over all 256 points (forward difference f(x+1) - f(x))"}, "files": [], "text": "monotonic 3x:\n  not monotonic on 0..255\n  maximal intervals of monotonicity:\n    x in 0..85: increasing\n    x in 85..86: decreasing\n    x in 86..170: increasing\n    x in 170..171: decreasing\n    x in 171..255: increasing\n  witness: x = 0 < x = 1 but f(0) = 0 < f(1) = 3 (not decreasing)\n  witness: x = 85 < x = 86 but f(85) = 255 > f(86) = 2 (not increasing)\n  note: without wrapping (as int) it is strictly increasing; the machine type wraps: f(85) = 255, f(86) = 2\n  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points (forward difference f(x+1) - f(x))\n"}
{"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "period", "ucas": "period sin(2x) + cos(3x)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "period", "var": "x", "status": "periodic", "period": {"value": 6.283185307179586, "exact": "2*pi"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi, cos(3x) has period 2*pi/3; p is their least common multiple; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)"}, "files": [], "text": "period of sin(2x) + cos(3x):\n  fundamental period 2*pi ≈ 6.283185307\n  proved symbolically: sin(2x) has period pi, cos(3x) has period 2*pi/3; p is their least common multiple; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)\n"}
